  "id": "23a36027-480c-56d6-9919-889e2fcac588",
  "slug": "monster-cookie-snack-cake-recipe-11973874",
  "name": "Monster Cookie Snack Cake",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "With peanut butter, oats, chocolate chips, and M&M'S, this cake is sure to be a crowd pleaser. Decorated to resemble a soccer pitch\u2014it\u2019ll be a surefire hit at your next watch party!",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Mix together oats and hot water in a small bowl. Set aside to soften for 20 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (80 degrees F). Grease a 9x13-inch pan and line the bottom with parchment paper."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "In a large bowl, whisk together melted butter, oil, peanut butter, brown sugar, salt, cinnamon, nutmeg, eggs, 1 tablespoon vanilla extract, and almond extract until smooth and combined, 1 to 2 minutes. Add in the oat mixture and sour cream, and whisk until thoroughly incorporated. Add in flour, baking powder, and baking soda, and whisk until just combined. Stir in 3/4 cup M&M'S and chocolate chips."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Pour batter into the prepared pan and smooth into an even layer. Bake until a toothpick inserted into the center of the cake comes out clean, 35 to 40 minutes. Allow the cake to cool in the pan for 15 minutes before removing to a wire rack to cool completely."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "To make the frosting, beat together softened butter and cream cheese until smooth and combined. Add in powdered sugar, 1 teaspoon vanilla extract, and pinch of salt and beat until thoroughly incorporated and frosting becomes smooth, 2 to 3 minutes. Measure out 1/4 cup of the frosting and set aside. To the remaining frosting, add green food coloring and mix until thoroughly incorporated."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Place cooled cake on a cake plate or serving platter. Frost the top of the cake with the green frosting. Place the reserved 1/4 cup frosting into a piping bag fitted with a small round tip. Pipe lines on top of the green frosting to resemble a soccer pitch. Arrange 16 M&M'S on the cake to resemble soccer players."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "When ready to serve, cut the cake into 32 pieces. Keep extra cake stored in an airtight container."
    }
  ],
